    "body": "Bug not reproducible on MacOS Catalina, using iTerm2 with zsh. Here's what I believe to be happening: Starship's init script inserts the bash function `starship_preexec()` before each shell token. Since `$_` expands into the name of the previous command, it appears to be possible that the `$_` is only expanded into its full form *after* the application of this `starship_preexec()` function, therefore returning that function name (which precedes each token, including `$_`). One workaround may be to replace `$_` with `${!_}`, but I have not tested this.",
